  "text_md": "# Med 3-4 Academic Program Committee Meeting Minutes 12/21/2009\n\n## Program Committee Student Rep Attendance\n\nArnold, Mark √ Khandelwal, Sorabh Bashaw, Hillary Barin, Kamrin √ Kman, Nicholas Fu, Julia Bartholomew, Deb √ Ledford, Cindy √ Gerstman, Jacob Presiding Chair: Mary McIlroy, MD Bourekas, Eric Letson, Alan Ho, Vincent √ Bowyer, Brian Liston, Beth House, Melissa Recording Secretary: Sean Bragg Clinchot, Dan Lynn, Joanne Rose, Maggie √ Cohen, Dan √ McIlroy, Mary Sauers, Lynn Call To Order: 4:07 pm √ Cronau, Holly Muscarella, Pete Schroeder, Catherine Ecklar, Pat Niedermier, Julie Subbarao, Catherine Adjourned: 5:30 Essig, Garth O'Dorisio, Nathan √ Tam, Marty Harzman, Alan Pfeil, Sheryl Vogt, Keith Location: B124 Graves Hall √ Hasbrouck, Carol Rose, Stephen Voss, Sarah √ Hoyle, Chad Scharschmidt, Thomas √ Wolfson, Anna Kapoor, Ritu Shim, Rosemarie\n\n## AGENDA DISCUSSIONS and CONCLUSIONS ACTIONS / FOLLOW-UP\n\n## I. Opening\n\nA. Approval of Minutes: November 16, 2009 meeting minutes approved.\nB. Announcements: a. Dr. Kman new Clerkship Director for DOC-1.\nb. Dr. Khandelwal new Assoc Director of Med 3-4.\nc. Faculty Development brochure \"Teaching for Optimal Patient Care with Electronic Medical Records\" printed and available for distribution to dept faculty.\n## II. Business\n\nA. CAPS presentation: The Clinical Assessment and Problem Solving (CAPS) program CAPS will take information gathered and discuss at\nrepresentatives gave an overview of their current Med 1-2 future APC meetings. They will return february or curriculum (handout). They listed some suggestions for how CAPS march to the Med 3-4 APC meeting to propose ideas. could function in the 3rd and 4th years, and opened the floor for discussion.\n",
